    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678-a2">

                <pb facs="1081" n="945" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg945"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 222.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Margron.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-11-15"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 15, 1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 95.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of yours of this date,
                    wherein you state that you do not hesitate to refer the case of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Haytian Republic</hi> to the judgment of the Government
                    of the United States, and express a desire so to do since we have already had
                    two conferences <pb facs="1082" n="946" xml:id="pg946"/> on this subject, and
                    without any result whatever. After mature consideration of the question and
                    consultation with Capt. F. M. Ramsay, of the United States ship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Boston</hi>, I have decided to comply with your request,
                    and will therefore communicate to my Government, by the first opportunity, the
                    tenor of your dispatch.</p>
                <p>I hereby call to your attention the fact that one of the crew of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Haytian Republic</hi> died last evening, and that others
                    are sick on board; in consequence I must request that such crew be turned over
                    to my care, that I may embark them by the first opportunity to the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>It is understood that the authorities taking charge of the steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Haytian Republic</hi> are responsible to the United
                    States Government for the same.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, the assurance of my distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. W.
                                Thompson</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                            Prince.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
